    "introduction": "Melrose Industries operates in aerospace through businesses that develop and manufacture components and systems for aircraft and engines. Its activities include engine structures and parts, airframe components and electrical systems for civil and defence applications. Customers include major aircraft and engine manufacturers, with programmes often lasting many years. Revenue comes from production work and, in parts of the engine business, aftermarket-related activity. Its model depends on engineering qualifications, manufacturing precision and long-term positions on aircraft programmes. Demand is influenced by aircraft build rates and fleet usage, while supply-chain reliability, production efficiency and investment in new technologies determine how effectively orders become earnings.",
